## 4. Default Values & Sizing Inspection

Variables declared without an explicit initial value (such as class fields) automatically take their type's **default value**:

| Type | Default Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| All Integral Types (`byte`, `int`, etc.) | `0` |
| Floating-Point Types (`float`, `double`) | `0.0` |
| `decimal` | `0.0m` |
| `bool` | `false` |
| `char` | `'\0'` (Null character) |
| All Reference Types (`string`, `class`, arrays) | `null` |

```csharp
// Inspecting sizes and limits using built-in C# operators
Console.WriteLine(sizeof(int));        // 4 (bytes)
Console.WriteLine(int.MinValue);       // -2147483648
Console.WriteLine(int.MaxValue);       // 2147483647
Console.WriteLine(default(decimal));   // 0
